I revived @javilopen's 28-year-old custom map for Quake II and turned it into a web-based version with Fable on fast mode. It took some hacking to fix texture loading issues by repacking PAK files, but now it works. AI is so good at restoring old files from backups; I was waiting for a backup app to browse my old data, and now AI makes it possible.

@javilopen made this map years ago, and with some help from Claude Fable, I managed to render it and run it in Quake II again. It brought back memories of hours spent noclipping in front of a PC. You can see the gameplay and textures in the images and video linked.

You can also play Quake II multiplayer online at q2.pieter.com, which offers low-latency, no-install multiplayer with client-side prediction.
